# Next.js server-first

## Architecture
- **Server Components by default.** Add `'use client'` only for real interactivity; push
  client boundaries to the leaves.
- **Thin transport:** Server Actions and Route Handlers do parse (Zod) -> invoke
  action/server function -> serialize. **No business logic in the transport layer.**
- `src/lib/<feature>/` suffixes: `*-server.ts` (reads, owns Drizzle queries), `*-actions.ts`
  (`'use server'` mutations - one entry point, Zod input, typed output with an explicit
  failure variant), `*-schemas.ts` (Zod), `*-display.ts` (pure formatting), `*-permissions.ts`.
- Components never import Drizzle; only `*-server.ts` / `*-actions.ts` / `src/lib/db` do.
- **Authorization is server-side** (field + row level), including exports. Sensitive data
  (salaries, loaded cost, reference TJM, margin) is filtered before serialization, never only
  hidden in the UI.

## UI/UX
- Every screen handles **loading, empty, success, error** explicitly; distinguish "empty"
  from "no results after filtering". No silent failures; contextual error copy.
- Destructive/state-changing actions require a confirmation dialog. Mutations disable the
  trigger and show loading.
- Forms: React Hook Form + Zod resolver, validation on blur, accessible labels.
- Tables/lists are server-driven (pagination/search/sort); filter state lives in the URL.
- Professional French UI, no emoji, no em dash. Deterministic rendering.
